+# Detailed Changes: Automatic Scaling/Complexity Gate Implementation
+
+## Files Changed
+
+### 1. NEW: `tools/check_scaling.py` (194 lines)
+
+**Purpose**: Validate that a solution's runtime scales appropriately for maximum constraints.
+
+**Key Functions**:
+- `tool_info()`: Returns tool metadata with JSON schema
+- `tool_function()`: Main validation logic
+
+**Input Parameters**:
+- `solution_path` (string): Path to solution.py
+- `generator_path` (string): Path to gen_scaled.py (accepts N as argv[1])
+- `max_n` (integer): Maximum N from constraints
+- `time_limit_sec` (float, default 2.0): Time budget for solve
+- `per_run_timeout` (float, default 10.0): Timeout per run
+
+**Algorithm**:
+1. Generate geometric series of sizes: max_n/1000, /300, /100, /30, /10, /3, 1x
+2. Run solution at each size, measure time
+3. Stop at first timeout
+4. Fit log-log regression on last 2-3 successful points
+5. Extrapolate runtime to max_n
+6. Return table, exponent, projected time, and verdict
+
+**Output Examples**:
+- `SCALING PASS (exponent=1.05, projected 0.8s at N=200000)`
+- `SCALING FAIL (exponent=2.1, projected 45.2s at N=200000, exceeds 2.0s limit)`
+
+### 2. MODIFIED: `tools/run_tests.py` (354 lines, +13 lines net)
+
+**Changes**:
+
+#### a) Distinct Seeds Per Iteration
+```python
+# OLD: run generator without seeding
+gen_result = subprocess.run(["python3", str(generator_path)], ...)
+
+# NEW: pass iteration index and SEED env var
+env = os.environ.copy()
+env['SEED'] = str(test_num)
+gen_result = subprocess.run(
+    ["python3", str(generator_path), str(test_num)],
+    env=env,
+    ...
+)
+```
+
+**Impact**: Each iteration generates different test cases instead of identical ones.
+
+#### b) Identical Input Detection
+```python
+# Track inputs in a set
+generated_inputs = set()
+generated_inputs.add(test_input)
+
+# After all tests, check if all identical
+if len(generated_inputs) == 1:
+    result_msg = f"⚠️ WARNING: All {num_iterations} generated inputs were IDENTICAL! ..."
+```
+
+**Impact**: Detects broken generators that ignore seeding.
+
+#### c) Prominent Max Input Warning
+```python
+# OLD: "WARNING: no max-size timing test was run"
+
+# NEW: "⚠️ WARNING: no max-size timing test was run (provide max_input_path for this)"
+```
+
+**Impact**: More visible reminder to test max constraints.
+
+### 3. MODIFIED: `coding_agent.py` (404 lines, ~120 lines added to forward())
+
+**Workflow Changes**:
+
+#### Phase 1 (Unchanged)
+- Initial solution
+- Sample testing
+- Complexity analysis
+
+#### Phase 1.5 (NEW)
+- Agent creates `gen_scaled.py` (worst-case generator for size N)
+- Agent states `max_n` from constraints
+- Agent runs `check_scaling` tool
+
+#### Scaling Validation Loop (NEW)
+```python
+max_scaling_rounds = 4
+scaling_passed = False
+
+for scaling_round in range(max_scaling_rounds):
+    if "SCALING PASS" in scaling_round_result:
+        scaling_passed = True
+        break
+    
+    if scaling_round < max_scaling_rounds - 1:
+        # Ask for algorithmic redesign
+        redesign_instruction = """Your algorithm is asymptotically too slow...
+        Do NOT attempt micro-optimization. You must redesign...
+        Consider: Prefix sums, hash maps, two-pointers, sorting+binary search, 
+        monotonic stack/deque, segment trees, divide-and-conquer, FFT"""
+        scaling_round_result = chat_with_agent(redesign_instruction, ...)
+    else:
+        return  # Give up after max rounds
+```
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Bounded (max 4 rounds)
+- Forbids micro-optimization
+- Suggests structural techniques
+- Only continues if "SCALING PASS" not achieved
+- Returns early if can't achieve scaling pass
+
+#### Phase 2 (After Scaling Passes)
+- Now ONLY runs after SCALING PASS confirmed
+- Creates brute.py (reference implementation)
+- Creates gen.py (with proper seeding documentation)
+- Runs differential testing with run_tests
+- Optional checker.py for multi-answer problems
+
+**Seeding Instructions for Agent**:
+```
+The generator MUST accept the iteration index as argv[1] (passed by run_tests for seeding)
+Use SEED environment variable or argv[1] to seed the random generator 
+(import os; seed = int(os.environ.get('SEED', '0')))
+```
+
+#### Review Loop (Bounded)
+```python
+max_review_rounds = 3
+
+for review_round in range(max_review_rounds):
+    if "ALL PASSED" in review_result:
+        break  # Done!
+    elif review_round < max_review_rounds - 1:
+        # Continue to next round
+```
+
+**Key Features**:
+- Bounded (max 3 rounds)
+- Exits early on "ALL PASSED"
+- Fixes issues and re-tests
+
+## Control Flow Diagram
+
+```
+START
+  |
+  v
+[Phase 1: Sample Testing]
+  |
+  v
+[Phase 1.5: Create gen_scaled.py & state max_n]
+  |
+  v
+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+| Scaling Validation Loop (max 4 rounds)      |
+|                                             |
+| [Run check_scaling]                         |
+|     |                                       |
+|     +---> "SCALING PASS" --> Go to Phase 2  |
+|     |                                       |
+|     +---> "SCALING FAIL" --> [Redesign] --> |
+|                              [Loop back]    |
+|                                             |
+| After 4 rounds: return (give up)            |
+└─────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+  |
+  v
+[Phase 2: Create brute.py, gen.py, checker.py (optional)]
+  |
+  v
+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
+| Differential Testing Loop (max 3 rounds)     |
+|                                              |
+| [Run run_tests]                              |
+|     |                                        |
+|     +---> "ALL PASSED" --> Done!             |
+|     |                                        |
+|     +---> Tests fail --> [Fix] --> [Loop]   |
+│                                              |
+| After 3 rounds: done                        |
+└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
+  |
+  v
+END
+```
+
+## Key Invariants
+
+1. **Scaling Before Differential Testing**
+   - Impossible to run run_tests before SCALING PASS
+   - Ensures no slow solutions enter differential testing
+
+2. **Bounded Loops**
+   - No `while True` loops
+   - All loops have explicit max iterations
+   - Clear exit conditions
+
+3. **Distinct Seeding**
+   - Each test iteration gets different seed
+   - Generator receives both argv[1] and SEED env var
+   - Cannot produce identical inputs by accident
+
+4. **Algorithmic Redesign Only**
+   - Prompt explicitly forbids micro-optimization
+   - Must identify structural bottleneck
+   - Must apply standard technique
+
+5. **Repository Awareness**
+   - All instructions mention `git_tempdir`
+   - Agent knows where to place files
+   - No confusion about working directory
+
+## Example Scenarios
+
+### Scenario 1: O(N^2) Solution
+1. Agent writes solution and passes samples
+2. Agent creates gen_scaled.py
+3. Agent runs check_scaling
+4. Result: `SCALING FAIL (exponent=1.95, projected 50000s at N=200000)`
+5. Loop: Agent must redesign (not micro-optimize)
+6. Agent identifies: "Inner loop over all j causes O(N^2)"
+7. Agent redesigns with hash map: O(N) amortized
+8. Agent runs check_scaling again
+9. Result: `SCALING PASS (exponent=1.0, projected 0.8s at N=200000)`
+10. Agent proceeds to differential testing
+11. All tests pass, solution is accepted
+
+### Scenario 2: O(N) Solution
+1. Agent writes solution and passes samples
+2. Agent creates gen_scaled.py
+3. Agent runs check_scaling
+4. Result: `SCALING PASS (exponent=1.0, projected 0.5s at N=200000)`
+5. Agent proceeds to differential testing
+6. Creates brute.py, gen.py, runs run_tests
+7. All tests pass, solution is accepted
+
+### Scenario 3: Broken Generator
+1. gen.py always outputs same case (bug)
+2. run_tests detects: `⚠️ WARNING: All 100 generated inputs were IDENTICAL!`
+3. Agent fixes generator to use SEED
+4. re-run: Different inputs produced
+5. Differential testing proceeds
+
+## Complexity Analysis
+
+### check_scaling Performance
+- Runs ~7 sizes (geometric series)
+- Each run: O(N) solution time + overhead
+- Total time: O(sum of run times) ≤ 20 seconds for reasonable algorithms
+- With 2s time limit, stops early on TLE
+
+### run_tests Performance
+- 100 iterations × (gen time + solution time + brute time)
+- With proper timeouts, bounded to 5-10 seconds total
+- Identical input detection is O(N) space for N iterations
+
+### coding_agent Performance
+- 4 scaling rounds × 2 min agent time = 8 minutes max
+- 3 review rounds × 2 min agent time = 6 minutes max
+- Total agent time: ~14 minutes for complete solution
+
+## Testing Coverage
+
+✅ Detects O(N^2) as SCALING FAIL
+✅ Detects O(N) as SCALING PASS
+✅ Detects identical inputs
+✅ Proper seed handling
+✅ Bounded loops
+✅ No micro-optimization allowed
+✅ Scaling before differential testing
+✅ All syntax valid
+✅ Schemas correct
+✅ Integration complete
+
