+# Implementation Summary: Automatic Scaling/Complexity Gate
+
+## Changes Made
+
+### 1. New Tool: `tools/check_scaling.py`
+- **Purpose**: Validate that a solution's runtime scales appropriately for maximum constraints
+- **Inputs**:
+  - `solution_path`: Path to the solution.py file to test
+  - `generator_path`: Path to gen_scaled.py script (accepts N as argv[1])
+  - `max_n`: Maximum N from problem constraints
+  - `time_limit_sec`: Time limit for full solve (default: 2.0s)
+  - `per_run_timeout`: Timeout per individual run (default: 10.0s)
+- **Behavior**:
+  - Runs solution at geometrically increasing sizes: max_n/1000, /300, /100, /30, /10, /3, 1x
+  - Stops at first timeout
+  - Records timing at each size
+  - Fits log-log slope on last 2-3 successful points
+  - Extrapolates runtime to max_n
+  - Returns table of measurements, estimated exponent, projected time, and verdict
+- **Output**: Contains either "SCALING PASS" or "SCALING FAIL"
+
+### 2. Updated: `tools/run_tests.py`
+- **Distinct Seeds per Iteration**:
+  - Each generator invocation now receives the iteration index as argv[1]
+  - Also passes SEED environment variable for proper random seeding
+  - This ensures generator produces different inputs each iteration
+  
+- **Identical Input Detection**:
+  - Tracks all generated inputs using a set
+  - Warns prominently if all generated inputs are identical
+  - Warning: "⚠️ WARNING: All N generated inputs were IDENTICAL!"
+  
+- **Prominent Max Input Warning**:
+  - Updated warning from plain text to "⚠️ WARNING:" format
+  - More visible reminder to provide max_input_path
+
+### 3. Updated: `coding_agent.py` forward() method
+- **New Workflow**:
+  1. **Phase 1**: Initial solution + sample testing (unchanged)
+  2. **Phase 1.5 (NEW)**: Scaling validation
+     - Agent creates gen_scaled.py (worst-case generator)
+     - Agent states max_n from constraints
+     - Runs check_scaling tool
+     - Bounded loop (max 4 rounds) for redesign iterations
+     
+  3. **Scaling Loop** (up to 4 rounds):
+     - If "SCALING PASS": proceed to Phase 2
+     - If "SCALING FAIL": demand algorithmic redesign (not micro-optimization)
+     - Provide suggestions for techniques: prefix sums, hash maps, two-pointers, sorting+binary search, monotonic stack/deque, segment trees, divide-and-conquer, FFT
+     - Only exits when "SCALING PASS" is seen
+     
+  4. **Phase 2**: Differential testing (only after scaling passes)
+     - Brute force implementation
+     - Random test generator (with proper seeding support)
+     - Comprehensive differential testing
+     - Fixes any issues found
+     
+  5. **Review Loop** (max 3 rounds):
+     - Re-run tests until "ALL PASSED" is seen
+     - Exit early when both conditions met (was: both "ALL PASSED" and "OK in"; now: just "ALL PASSED" since scaling already validated)
+
+- **Key Constraint**: No while True loops, all loops are bounded
